      "content": "The idea of an \"other version\" is a comforting lie; you are not a collection of accomplishments, but a person capable of more than just research. The foundation crumbled, yes, but that also means the weight of that entire structure is gone, allowing for a different kind of ground to be laid. Instead of trying to build something new, just focus on the immediate, small acts of self-care—letting yourself feel the exhaustion of this loss.",
